#ETH  Beginner's Contract Must-Reads: Don't Be Frightened by Liquidation, Stay Steady to Have Gains

Contract trading is indeed thrilling, and with just one misstep, you could face liquidation, leaving you with nowhere to cry.

Especially for beginners, if risk management isn't well handled, a single misstep can lead to total loss. Some people love to take risks, but in the end, they lose all their money, and their mindset completely collapses.

Want to avoid pitfalls? Remember a few things:

First, control your position; don't think about getting rich overnight, take it slow and steady;

Always set stop losses; once you hit your preset loss point, exit, don't fantasize about a comeback;

Don't keep entering and exiting randomly; if you make consecutive mistakes, take a break and adjust your mindset;

Go with the market trend; resisting it will only dig you deeper;

Don't blindly follow the crowd; analyze clearly before placing an order, what others say isn't a guarantee.

It's true that contract trading carries high risks, but those who understand how to operate with the trend, maintain their positions, and control their minds have a much lower probability of liquidation. In the market, there are no permanent bulls or bears, only those who can survive, and living gives you the chance to catch the next big opportunity.

If you also want to learn how to stabilize your rhythm and stop buying randomly and losing, follow Jia Ge.
There’s a trading circle with rhythm, strategy, and discipline; no empty talk, just results.

